{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` requires a plan-review attestation for a bug fix over 150 non-test lines. When the attestation classification itself raises (`classify_plan_review_attestation` catches every exception and returns `verdict: \"error\"`), `apply_bugfix_size_gate` maps INFRA to an **advisory** finding (module docstring: \"Fail-open on infrastructure\") and the change keeps `LLM-Review +1`. An infrastructure fault therefore produces the same outcome as a satisfied gate.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Gerrit change 1369 (`73abb5805f`, trailer ticket e39f, type bug, 525 non-test lines) merged on `LLM-Review +1` with 0 blocking / 2 advisory findings; the REVIEW_RESULT coverage records the bugfix-size gate as `error`. The ticket `asbestos-lithe-kouprey` (b6e1-c217-8cd3-4446) was later filed against that change.\n- Unit: make `_load_ticket_state` raise inside `classify_plan_review_attestation`; `apply_bugfix_size_gate` leaves `verdict` unchanged from PASS.\n\n## Expected\nAn infrastructure error in a blocking gate abstains instead of passing: the verdict becomes INDETERMINATE, with the classification error surfaced in the coverage record (`coverage.bugfix_size_gate.verdict == \"error\"`). Downstream (existing behaviour, unchanged by this fix): the review-bot adapter maps a non-PASS verdict with no blocking findings to the `indeterminate` coverage gap and the voter casts the fail-closed `-1` tagged as infrastructure — never a `+1` — so an unclassifiable oversized bug fix can no longer merge on the gate's silence. This is the same fail-closed-on-infra posture the codebase already established (bug 3fce: an unreadable ruling is an error, never a silent degrade; WS5 `detectors.apply_failclosed`).\n\n## Approach\nChange only the INFRA arm of `apply_bugfix_size_gate`: instead of appending an advisory finding, set `verdict[\"verdict\"] = \"INDETERMINATE\"` (never downgrading an existing BLOCK). The coverage entry (already written for every bucket) keeps carrying the `error` verdict and reason, so the bot's infra-recovery/retrigger loop can observe why. Leave the `flag` (BLOCK) and `accepted` (no-op) arms, the ≤150-line no-op, and the missing-trailer no-op unchanged. Update the module docstring (`Fail-open on infrastructure` → fail-closed abstain), `bucket_for_verdict`'s docstring, and the stale caller comment in `finalize.py`.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` — the INFRA arm + docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` — the call-site comment only.\n- `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` — new RED test for the INDETERMINATE outcome; rewrite the two tests that encoded the old fail-open behaviour (`test_infra_or_unknown_classification_is_advisory_never_blocks`, `test_classifier_exception_degrades_to_advisory`); a guard test that an already-BLOCK verdict is not downgraded.\n\n## Testing\n- RED first: classification error on a >150-line non-test bug-fix diff yields `verdict == \"INDETERMINATE\"`, a coverage entry `bugfix_size_gate.verdict == \"error\"` / `bucket == \"infra\"`, and no advisory or blocking finding that reads as a pass.\n- Edge: an infra classification when the verdict is already BLOCK leaves BLOCK in place.\n- Unchanged behaviour: `unsigned`/`stale-material` still BLOCK, accepted verdicts still no-op, under-floor and test-only diffs never read the store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A classification error (both the classifier's own `error` verdict and an exception escaping to the gate's outer handler) on an over-floor bug fix produces an INDETERMINATE review verdict, not PASS; checked by the new unit tests in `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`.\n- [ ] An infra classification never downgrades an existing BLOCK verdict; checked by a new unit test.\n- [ ] Existing tests for `unsigned`, certified/stale-code/stale-head, under-floor, test-only, non-bug, and unresolvable-ticket behaviour pass unchanged; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`.\n- [ ] The Gerrit voter's existing INDETERMINATE handling (terminal fail-closed `-1`, no `+1`) is unchanged; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k indeterminate`.\n\n## Verification\n`pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k \"bugfix_size or indeterminate\"`; `make lint`; `make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787366975541717001,"uuid":"2a11a9c0-4644-4c2b-a153-3fdd402d981a"}